# Independently authored PG transaction-management
# admin-function sentinel slice for the GPL MTR-
# format runner. NOT copied or adapted from MySQL's
# mysql-test/.
#
# Existing coverage (do NOT duplicate):
#   - GET_LOCK / RELEASE_LOCK family: pinned at
#     pg_advisory_lock_basic_extra (mysql wire stubs
#     for the named-mutex equivalents).
#   - PG advisory_lock_basic_extra: pinned. Those are
#     a DIFFERENT family from the txn-management
#     admin fns covered here.
#   - txid_current / pg_current_xact_id /
#     pg_terminate_backend / pg_cancel_backend /
#     pg_blocking_pids / pg_xact_status /
#     pg_backend_pid / txid_status /
#     pg_my_temp_schema: ZERO prior coverage.
#
# Pre-existing rejection / behavior shape patterns:
#   - "execution error: unknown function: <name>" —
#     pre-existing fingerprint at many slices (e.g.,
#     pg_ordinality_match_reflection PR #408 for
#     to_regclass/regtype/regproc, pg_hypothetical_
#     within_group PR #412 for rank/dense_rank).
#     Reused for all 9 admin fns probed here.
#
# This slice pins:
#
#   Transaction-ID fns (PG snapshot-mgmt API):
#     - txid_current() — pre-PG13 name
#     - pg_current_xact_id() — PG13+ rename
#     - pg_xact_status(xid) — status of a given txid
#     - txid_status('xid') — pre-PG13 string-arg form
#     All four: "unknown function: <name>".
#
#   Backend/session-mgmt fns (PG cluster admin):
#     - pg_backend_pid() — current backend's PID
#     - pg_terminate_backend(pid) — SIGTERM a backend
#     - pg_cancel_backend(pid) — SIGINT a backend's
#       current query
#     - pg_blocking_pids(pid) — array of pids blocking
#       a given pid
#     All four: "unknown function: <name>". The
#     SECURITY-relevant fns (terminate/cancel) cannot
#     be invoked — silent absence means no admin
#     control surface, AND no abuse surface.
#
#   Schema-namespace fn:
#     - pg_my_temp_schema() — OID of session's temp
#       schema (PG returns 0 if none allocated yet).
#       "unknown function: pg_my_temp_schema".
#
# Big-picture finding:
#
#   PG transaction-management and backend-session
#   admin function families are entirely unreachable
#   on zeta. Apps porting PG observability /
#   monitoring tools that:
#     - Snapshot the current xid to correlate with
#       WAL records / CDC: use zeta's CDC stream
#       (logical replication) directly which already
#       embeds commit timestamps.
#     - Cancel/terminate runaway queries: use the
#       database-level connection close from the
#       client side; zeta has no SQL-level admin
#       surface to terminate other backends.
#     - Compute blocker chains for lock contention
#       diagnosis: not available; use pg_stat_*-style
#       observability via OS-level tools.
#
#   SECURITY-POSITIVE: silent absence of
#   pg_terminate_backend / pg_cancel_backend means
#   no SQL-level admin surface exists for these
#   privileged operations. Authentication-bypass via
#   SQL injection cannot escalate to backend-kill.
#
# Wire divergence check: probed both wires (pgwire
# port 13501 and mysqlwire port 3307) — identical
# "unknown function: <name>" fingerprint on every fn.
# Function lookup is at executor function-dispatch,
# wire-independent.
#
# Adaptation notes:
#   # zeta-adapt: KNOWN GAP — entire txid_* /
#     pg_current_xact_id / pg_xact_status family.
#     Apps using PG snapshot-management API for
#     observability should consume CDC stream
#     (commit timestamps embedded) instead.
#   # zeta-adapt: KNOWN GAP (security-positive) — no
#     pg_backend_pid / pg_terminate_backend /
#     pg_cancel_backend / pg_blocking_pids. No SQL-
#     level surface to inspect or kill other backends.
#   # zeta-adapt: KNOWN GAP — pg_my_temp_schema not
#     available. Use information_schema for
#     introspection of temp tables if needed.

--echo === Transaction-ID fns (snapshot-mgmt API) ===

--error 1105
SELECT txid_current();
--error 1105
SELECT pg_current_xact_id();
--error 1105
SELECT pg_xact_status(1);
--error 1105
SELECT txid_status('1');

--echo === Backend/session-mgmt fns (cluster admin) ===

--error 1105
SELECT pg_backend_pid();
--error 1105
SELECT pg_terminate_backend(123);
--error 1105
SELECT pg_cancel_backend(123);
--error 1105
SELECT pg_blocking_pids(123);

--echo === Schema-namespace fn ===

--error 1105
SELECT pg_my_temp_schema();
